comments.text:
@WesRoth - THE STAKES ARE HIGH.  One aspect of the research I didn't see from your walk-through of the paper was the lack of variability of patient behaviors, and their ability to relay accurate information about their conditions/diseases. Also, I didn't see the word emotion mentioned anywhere (did any of the agents get their medical license threatened by a screaming "Karen" patient with a lawyer husband, who doesn't even know where the pain is coming from?) 
Perhaps people have been sensitized through movies that show future worst-case interactions (I'm thinking of Elysium) where agents don't offer enough options, or understand nuance.
The reason this can be upsetting can include remembering the outcomes from incompetence of human doctors and the stakes involved when the doctors get to the "ABORT" step in the flowchart you showed from the paper.
